{"data": {"answers": {"trust: the Bash doors fail open on any multi-line command. guards.segments() treats a newline as whitespace, so 'true\\ngit push --force origin x' reads as one `true` command. Any unbalanced quote (an apostrophe in a heredoc body) makes it return nothing. This affects every door that reads Bash: force push, merge with gaps, gh api writes, PR create. It happened for real at 08:00:03, when the child's heredoc + `gh pr create` passed the create door before its gates counted. SECURITY.md puts this in scope and says to report it privately. How do we fix it? I recommend a private advisory and fork.": "Public PR now"}, "questions": ["trust: the Bash doors fail open on any multi-line command. guards.segments() treats a newline as whitespace, so 'true\\ngit push --force origin x' reads as one `true` command. Any unbalanced quote (an apostrophe in a heredoc body) makes it return nothing. This affects every door that reads Bash: force push, merge with gaps, gh api writes, PR create. It happened for real at 08:00:03, when the child's heredoc + `gh pr create` passed the create door before its gates counted. SECURITY.md puts this in scope and says to report it privately. How do we fix it? I recommend a private advisory and fork."]}, "hash": "8b4195644bd0c76dfb49282d93636d3ee32062675957ab668022830b3d268c9c", "kind": "prompt", "prev": "39efd66c96ddd926af201bedd1f320d7aa40bf837cb5deb5c57515d61260be28", "ts": "2026-10-16T08:19:06+00:00", "v": 1}
